dem-open-parens.gls -- dem-open-parens.scm

The file: 10 MB of ( on one line, and a newline.  No ) anywhere.  A
scanner that reads the text again from its start for every character, or
a display that scans the whole line for every key, takes seconds here.

Open:   chezweb dem-open-parens.scm

1. C-M-f                 at the start (Esc C-f)
   Expect: "No expression after the cursor", the cursor stays at the start,
   within 2 s (about 1.5 s in the cloud: the slowest key of all these tests).
2. C-M-b                 Expect: "No expression before the cursor", at once.
3. x                     Expect: an x at the start, at once.
4. M->                   to the end of the text (Esc >)
   Expect: the end of the long line on the screen, within 2 s.
5. C-M-b                 Expect: no expression before, at once.
6. y                     Expect: a y typed at the end, within 0.5 s.
7. DEL                   Expect: the y gone, within 0.5 s.
8. C-a  then  C-e        After M-> the cursor is on the empty line after
                         the final newline.  Expect: C-a and C-e leave it
                         there, at once.
8b. C-p  then  C-a  then  C-e
                         Expect: the last row of the long line; C-a and
                         C-e go to the start and the end of that row, at
                         once (they work on rows; M-x move-beginning-of-line
                         goes to the start of the whole line).
9. M-<                   Expect: back at the start, at once.
10. C-x k RET, then "y" if it asks: the text is changed, do not save it.
